(5140268, 748040, 67258, '<td valign="top">That is one impressive border!  Good clarity, super cheerful colours, and made me laugh.  Have to deduct a point or two for the lens flare on the shoe-horn, though!</td>', 'That is one impressive border!  Good clarity, super cheerful colours, and made me laugh.  Have to deduct a point or two for the lens flare on the shoe-horn, though!', '2008-12-19 06:22:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5140271, 747984, 67258, '<td valign="top">The colours are appealing, and i particularly like the effect of the out of focus drum on the right.  Overall, though, I find the photo too busy for my tastes, and wish the in focus ornament stood out more from the background.</td>', 'The colours are appealing, and i particularly like the effect of the out of focus drum on the right.  Overall, though, I find the photo too busy for my tastes, and wish the in focus ornament stood out more from the background.', '2008-12-19 06:25:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5140272, 747736, 67258, '<td valign="top">Spider on acid!  Very cool effect.</td>', 'Spider on acid!  Very cool effect.', '2008-12-19 06:25:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5140273, 746812, 67258, '<td valign="top">More a shallow depth of field than bokeh, to my mind.</td>', 'More a shallow depth of field than bokeh, to my mind.', '2008-12-19 06:26:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5140274, 747953, 67258, '<td valign="top">Lack of focus on your subject hurts this.  The concept is good, but some way to go with the technicals.  Looks like you may have converted to B&amp;W because the dog is suffering from ''green eye'' - one way to overcome that is to have the flash off-camera.  I also wonder if the composition could be improved by adopting a higher viewpoint.  as it is the viewer is looking up at the dog, which is slightly intimidating, and uncomfortable - you may want to explore taking portraits at eye level.  Keep practicing.</td>', 'Lack of focus on your subject hurts this.  The concept is good, but some way to go with the technicals.  Looks like you may have converted to B&W because the dog is suffering from ''green eye'' - one way to overcome that is to have the flash off-camera.  I also wonder if the composition could be improved by adopting a higher viewpoint.  as it is the viewer is looking up at the dog, which is slightly intimidating, and uncomfortable - you may want to explore taking portraits at eye level.  Keep practicing.', '2008-12-19 06:30:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5140278, 747329, 67258, '<td valign="top">Perfectly placed starburst, and the bokeh adds to the feeling of celebration and wonder.  Shame about the reflection of the door (?) on the bauble, but reflections on shiny curved surfaces are pretty much impossible to avoid - and you have done well not to get yourself in the shot!</td>', 'Perfectly placed starburst, and the bokeh adds to the feeling of celebration and wonder.  Shame about the reflection of the door (?) on the bauble, but reflections on shiny curved surfaces are pretty much impossible to avoid - and you have done well not to get yourself in the shot!', '2008-12-19 06:33:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5140279, 747898, 67258, '<td valign="top">Gentle and pleasing.</td>', 'Gentle and pleasing.', '2008-12-19 06:33:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5140280, 747750, 67258, '<td valign="top">The very cheerful and colourful bokeh, spread evenly throughout the photograph, gives a feeling of celebration and wonder.  The tilt lends just the right level of dynamism.</td>', 'The very cheerful and colourful bokeh, spread evenly throughout the photograph, gives a feeling of celebration and wonder.  The tilt lends just the right level of dynamism.', '2008-12-19 06:35:40.000000', NULL, 1),
