(5154441, 747946, 81530, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club... <br/> <br/>I was not able to vote on this challenge, but if I had, I probably would have given you a 7. <br/> <br/>Cassie, this is just beautiful. You have nice sharp detail on a couple of the berries/flowers, and the background is nice and soft. The square crop is great because it keeps our focus where it should be. The colours are very delicate overall, and you''ve finished it off with a nice frame. I really don''t have any constructive criticism. All in all, it''s a strong image. Congrats on your good finish and personal best!<br/> <br/>If you need any clarification on any of my comments, please feel free to pm me. It might take some time for me to get back to you.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club...  I was not able to vote on this challenge, but if I had, I probably would have given you a 7.  Cassie, this is just beautiful. You have nice sharp detail on a couple of the berries/flowers, and the background is nice and soft. The square crop is great because it keeps our focus where it should be. The colours are very delicate overall, and you''ve finished it off with a nice frame. I really don''t have any constructive criticism. All in all, it''s a strong image. Congrats on your good finish and personal best! If you need any clarification on any of my comments, please feel free to pm me. It might take some time for me to get back to you.', '2008-12-28 02:04:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5154445, 747108, 81530, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club... <br/> <br/>I was not able to vote on this challenge, but if I had, I probably would have given you a 6 or 7. <br/> <br/>My first thought is that I really like the composition you have chosen. I like how the cardinal just pops into the shot; it''s an unusual but interesting choice. The red really pops out against the green background. I also like all the negative space. It''s as if the bird is thinking or dreaming. There is not much to critique other than the border. I''m not a big fan of faded borders, but it is not overly distracting. Congrats on your top 25 finish.<br/> <br/>If you need any clarification on any of my comments, please feel free to pm me. It might take some time for me to get back to you.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club...  I was not able to vote on this challenge, but if I had, I probably would have given you a 6 or 7.  My first thought is that I really like the composition you have chosen. I like how the cardinal just pops into the shot; it''s an unusual but interesting choice. The red really pops out against the green background. I also like all the negative space. It''s as if the bird is thinking or dreaming. There is not much to critique other than the border. I''m not a big fan of faded borders, but it is not overly distracting. Congrats on your top 25 finish. If you need any clarification on any of my comments, please feel free to pm me. It might take some time for me to get back to you.', '2008-12-28 02:09:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5154451, 747948, 81530, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club... <br/> <br/>I was not able to vote on this challenge, but if I had, I probably would have given you a 5 or 6. <br/> <br/>My first impression is that I like the colours and contrast as they are very strong. The composition feels a little busy. The three most important pieces are the two in the foreground, and clear piece in the middleground. The pieces in the background are a little distracting. Perhaps if they were smaller pieces such as rooks, they would not grab our attention so much. I think the angle of the board has room for improvement as well. Rotating the board even more might give this shot a little more drama. Overall it is an interesting shot, it just needs some more thought to take it to the next level.<br/> <br/>If you need any clarification on any of my comments, please feel free to pm me. It might take some time for me to get back to you.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club...  I was not able to vote on this challenge, but if I had, I probably would have given you a 5 or 6.  My first impression is that I like the colours and contrast as they are very strong. The composition feels a little busy. The three most important pieces are the two in the foreground, and clear piece in the middleground. The pieces in the background are a little distracting. Perhaps if they were smaller pieces such as rooks, they would not grab our attention so much. I think the angle of the board has room for improvement as well. Rotating the board even more might give this shot a little more drama. Overall it is an interesting shot, it just needs some more thought to take it to the next level. If you need any clarification on any of my comments, please feel free to pm me. It might take some time for me to get back to you.', '2008-12-28 02:13:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5154458, 747354, 81530, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club... <br/> <br/>I was not able to vote on this challenge, but if I had, I probably would have given you a 6. <br/> <br/>My first thought is that you have some very nice bokeh in the background. The random spacing and colours of the ovals keep this interesting. The crop on the snowflake could use some work. I feel as if it was cropped to close to the bottom as we can see just the stub of the bottom leaf of the snowflake. Either moving the crop down, or raising the snowflake slightly higher would be an improvement in my opinion. I like all the details in the snow flake, and the subtle reflections are nice as well. The right hand side of the snowflake is noisy due to the low depth of field. I believe this is because your ISO was set to 1600. I''m assuming you could get the same bokeh effect using ISO 100 and a tripod.<br/> <br/>If you need any clarification on any of my comments, please feel free to pm me. It might take some time for me to get back to you.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club...  I was not able to vote on this challenge, but if I had, I probably would have given you a 6.  My first thought is that you have some very nice bokeh in the background. The random spacing and colours of the ovals keep this interesting. The crop on the snowflake could use some work. I feel as if it was cropped to close to the bottom as we can see just the stub of the bottom leaf of the snowflake. Either moving the crop down, or raising the snowflake slightly higher would be an improvement in my opinion. I like all the details in the snow flake, and the subtle reflections are nice as well. The right hand side of the snowflake is noisy due to the low depth of field. I believe this is because your ISO was set to 1600. I''m assuming you could get the same bokeh effect using ISO 100 and a tripod. If you need any clarification on any of my comments, please feel free to pm me. It might take some time for me to get back to you.', '2008-12-28 02:22:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5154464, 747524, 81530, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club... <br/> <br/>I was not able to vote on this challenge, but if I had, I probably would have given you a 6. <br/> <br/>My first thought is that the lighting is beautiful. The backlighting creates a very nice silhouette with lots of information. The exposure is very good as the highlights are not blow out, and you can clearly see the rim lighting. The out of focus background really separates the plant from the rest of the photograph. This really makes the viewer stay focused on the plant, and in that respect, the bokeh is actually functional. The background reminds me of a "Group of 7" painting. The photo is very good overall, and I don''t have anything to add that might improve this photograph. Great shot.<br/> <br/>If you need any clarification on any of my comments, please feel free to pm me. It might take some time for me to get back to you.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club...  I was not able to vote on this challenge, but if I had, I probably would have given you a 6.  My first thought is that the lighting is beautiful. The backlighting creates a very nice silhouette with lots of information. The exposure is very good as the highlights are not blow out, and you can clearly see the rim lighting. The out of focus background really separates the plant from the rest of the photograph. This really makes the viewer stay focused on the plant, and in that respect, the bokeh is actually functional. The background reminds me of a "Group of 7" painting. The photo is very good overall, and I don''t have anything to add that might improve this photograph. Great shot. If you need any clarification on any of my comments, please feel free to pm me. It might take some time for me to get back to you.', '2008-12-28 02:27:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(5154470, 747822, 81530, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club... <br/> <br/>I was not able to vote on this challenge, but if I had, I probably would have given you a 6 or 7. <br/> <br/>My first impression is, wow, why didn''t this score higher? A nice and clean composition with a wonderful variety of circles. I like to tell people they haven''t left enough breathing space for their subjects, but in this case, you have left enough room to make this work. I like that is not looking into the largest negative space, which is the crop chosen most often. Yes the highlights are a tad overexposed. I''m not saying a photograph has to have a perfect exposure, but in this case, I don''t think it adds anything to the photograph. All in all, a lovely photograph. Keep up the good work.<br/> <br/>If you need any clarification on any of my comments, please feel free to pm me. It might take some time for me to get back to you.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club...  I was not able to vote on this challenge, but if I had, I probably would have given you a 6 or 7.  My first impression is, wow, why didn''t this score higher? A nice and clean composition with a wonderful variety of circles. I like to tell people they haven''t left enough breathing space for their subjects, but in this case, you have left enough room to make this work. I like that is not looking into the largest negative space, which is the crop chosen most often. Yes the highlights are a tad overexposed. I''m not saying a photograph has to have a perfect exposure, but in this case, I don''t think it adds anything to the photograph. All in all, a lovely photograph. Keep up the good work. If you need any clarification on any of my comments, please feel free to pm me. It might take some time for me to get back to you.', '2008-12-28 02:32:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(5154573, 747011, 53316, '<td valign="top">Such a beautiful image. The subject and background compliment each other perfectly, not only with the color being the same, but also the way that the bokeh circles in the background match the circles on the ornament, *and* the variations in lightness and darkness within both elements.  This cohesiveness makes for a very stunning image.  To nitpick, I would have prefered even more symmetry to go with the symmetry I have already mentioned: the top of the ornament is not perfectly straight-on (it''s a horrible nitpick, really) and I would have enjoyed a square crop for symmetry which would also have gotten rid of the slightly distracting blur on the bottom left of the image.  But these, as I said, are nitpicks, which came to mind only because the rest of the image is absolutely perfect.</td>', 'Such a beautiful image. The subject and background compliment each other perfectly, not only with the color being the same, but also the way that the bokeh circles in the background match the circles on the ornament, *and* the variations in lightness and darkness within both elements.  This cohesiveness makes for a very stunning image.  To nitpick, I would have prefered even more symmetry to go with the symmetry I have already mentioned: the top of the ornament is not perfectly straight-on (it''s a horrible nitpick, really) and I would have enjoyed a square crop for symmetry which would also have gotten rid of the slightly distracting blur on the bottom left of the image.  But these, as I said, are nitpicks, which came to mind only because the rest of the image is absolutely perfect.', '2008-12-28 08:03:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5154576, 747105, 53316, '<td valign="top">Oh how lovely! I could totally see this on the front of a Christmas card - with a little bit of lightening of the subject, this would be perfect in my opinion. I don''t know how you''d go about selling something to a card company but at least you should make a print because it seems to me to be a very markatable image.  I can just smell the pine and cinnamon!</td>', 'Oh how lovely! I could totally see this on the front of a Christmas card - with a little bit of lightening of the subject, this would be perfect in my opinion. I don''t know how you''d go about selling something to a card company but at least you should make a print because it seems to me to be a very markatable image.  I can just smell the pine and cinnamon!', '2008-12-28 08:06:17.000000', NULL, 0),
