(5155216, 747779, 58785, '<td valign="top">Hello from Critique Club ;)<br/> <br/>Chris, when I click that button says "Gimme an image to Critique" each time I hope to get photos like yours. It is very pleasing to look at your images, you are doing great job with humans, portraits... although your blue is a vase, it doesn''t matter.<br/> <br/>This photo, Technically very very good. I see absolutely no place that shines to burn my eyes, yet no place dark enough to take the attention away. It is very sharp and clean photo.<br/> <br/>Composition is also very well done. The angle and the framing of your dad is right on the spot.<br/> <br/>I really don''t give a you know what for the subject of the challenge, but I certainly see "bokeh" here. Top right corner has all the bokeh one must see to vote nicely.<br/> <br/>2s and 3s are not justifying this photo at all. No matter who says what, I am totally against the "Low Voters" mentality, they are just bunch of crackheads "think" they know something about photography... which they all should go a flip burgers, and give their cameras to someone who would understand photography :(<br/> <br/>Good job, keep them coming.<br/> <br/>Leo</td>', 'Hello from Critique Club ;) Chris, when I click that button says "Gimme an image to Critique" each time I hope to get photos like yours. It is very pleasing to look at your images, you are doing great job with humans, portraits... although your blue is a vase, it doesn''t matter. This photo, Technically very very good. I see absolutely no place that shines to burn my eyes, yet no place dark enough to take the attention away. It is very sharp and clean photo. Composition is also very well done. The angle and the framing of your dad is right on the spot. I really don''t give a you know what for the subject of the challenge, but I certainly see "bokeh" here. Top right corner has all the bokeh one must see to vote nicely. 2s and 3s are not justifying this photo at all. No matter who says what, I am totally against the "Low Voters" mentality, they are just bunch of crackheads "think" they know something about photography... which they all should go a flip burgers, and give their cameras to someone who would understand photography :( Good job, keep them coming. Leo', '2008-12-28 17:16:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5155236, 746812, 58785, '<td valign="top">Hello from Critique Club ;)<br/> <br/>Steve, this is a nice photo, I like the way birds are having some sort of chaos. I can certainly "hear" the birds from this photo. There are some things that I wish weren''t there such as the bird all the way bottom left corner, and right side is a bit spacey for the whole picture.<br/> <br/>Colors are nice, focus right on the spot, both birds in the background and foreground is giving 3D feeling to the whole image, very nice. You were bombed by voters who thinks this is not a Bokeh image, which they might be right. There is a lot of confusion about "What is Bokeh" anyway...<br/> <br/>It''s a nice catch, honestly though if I did vote I probably would give you around 3 maybe 4. Even it''s a nice photo, 1-doesn''t give me the bokeh feeling too much, and 2-it''s just an ordinary shot of some birds :(<br/> <br/>I see you are an animal shooter, and had only 2 entries since 2004. I don''t care why, but you should enter more challenges as much as possible. Your scores should go up not go down yet still much better than my first two challenges :P<br/> <br/>Good luck on your next :)<br/> <br/>Leo</td>', 'Hello from Critique Club ;) Steve, this is a nice photo, I like the way birds are having some sort of chaos. I can certainly "hear" the birds from this photo. There are some things that I wish weren''t there such as the bird all the way bottom left corner, and right side is a bit spacey for the whole picture. Colors are nice, focus right on the spot, both birds in the background and foreground is giving 3D feeling to the whole image, very nice. You were bombed by voters who thinks this is not a Bokeh image, which they might be right. There is a lot of confusion about "What is Bokeh" anyway... It''s a nice catch, honestly though if I did vote I probably would give you around 3 maybe 4. Even it''s a nice photo, 1-doesn''t give me the bokeh feeling too much, and 2-it''s just an ordinary shot of some birds :( I see you are an animal shooter, and had only 2 entries since 2004. I don''t care why, but you should enter more challenges as much as possible. Your scores should go up not go down yet still much better than my first two challenges :P Good luck on your next :) Leo', '2008-12-28 17:29:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5155373, 747924, 47852, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>First Impression:  A good use of the shallow dof to bring attention to the cat''s head, but it''s still difficult to see the cat clearly due to the lighting.  I''m not sure that the bokeh adds to the overall photo, in fact the lines and color seem to help the cat blend in a bit.  All that being said, I like the composition and the feel you captured with the cat finding the last little bit of sunshine on the floor to nap in.  I doubt though that this did very well during voting because it doesn''t have the DPC mass appeal.<br/> <br/>After reading comments and info:  Not quite sure what aperture you used here... it says f/ 1.2 but that doesn''t work with the lens you listed.  I think if you had added a bit of reflected light back towards his face, it would have evened out the lighting a bit, but still giving you the bokeh in the background.  You may have been able to bump the ISO to 400 too, giving you a bit less noise and maybe a smoother background.<br/> <br/>Hope this has been helpful!  Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! First Impression:  A good use of the shallow dof to bring attention to the cat''s head, but it''s still difficult to see the cat clearly due to the lighting.  I''m not sure that the bokeh adds to the overall photo, in fact the lines and color seem to help the cat blend in a bit.  All that being said, I like the composition and the feel you captured with the cat finding the last little bit of sunshine on the floor to nap in.  I doubt though that this did very well during voting because it doesn''t have the DPC mass appeal. After reading comments and info:  Not quite sure what aperture you used here... it says f/ 1.2 but that doesn''t work with the lens you listed.  I think if you had added a bit of reflected light back towards his face, it would have evened out the lighting a bit, but still giving you the bokeh in the background.  You may have been able to bump the ISO to 400 too, giving you a bit less noise and maybe a smoother background. Hope this has been helpful!  Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions.', '2008-12-28 19:53:31.000000', NULL, 0),
